  "interpretation": "Published routers (RouterGNN message-passing, AD-GNN per-node depth via signal preservation) scored on the same frozen routing-blind k-means pool and splits as every baseline. RouterGNN shares the MLP gate's cross-fit supervision; AD-GNN is label-free. The message-passing router is trained with LayerNorm, weight decay and gradient clipping (the raw unnormalized stack diverges on large graphs); loss first->last, router fit accuracy and distinct channels emitted are recorded per run so a collapsed router is never silently reported as a trained one. Significance is a paired Wilcoxon signed-rank test of per-split means (router minus no-routing); win-counts alone are not evidence."
